                    "patching_rect": [ 145.0, 1207.0, 375.0, 24.0 ],
                    "text": "In the Live session, go to Arrangement View (press Tab) and Play."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "bgcolor": [ 1.0, 0.788235, 0.470588, 1.0 ],
                    "fontname": "Arial Bold",
                    "hint": "",
                    "id": "obj-69",
                    "ignoreclick": 1,
                    "legacytextcolor": 1,
                    "maxclass": "textbutton",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 3,
                    "outlettype": [ "", "", "int" ],
                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 1039.0, 895.0, 23.0, 21.0 ],
                    "rounded": 60.0,
                    "text": "4b",
                    "textcolor": [ 0.34902, 0.34902, 0.34902, 1.0 ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-68",
                    "linecount": 6,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 1064.0, 766.0, 248.0, 87.0 ],
                    "text": "Note that there are 4 videoSync devices already set. Each device has it's \"prepend message\" option on, which we use to prepend a name to all outcoming messages. Like this we can keep all devices properly separated without cross-talking/triggering."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "bubble": 1,
                    "id": "obj-66",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 1064.0, 718.0, 247.0, 37.0 ],
                    "text": "Open the syncSuite-tutorial1.als session in the /ableton-project folder."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "bubble": 1,
                    "id": "obj-65",
                    "linecount": 7,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 698.0, 875.0, 247.0, 104.0 ],
                    "text": "What is happening inside here is just an extra step to get the correct video paths from the Live project folder. This is not necessary when working with your own computer and paths. But it's good to know in case of needing to export the project elsewhere/remap the video paths."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-64",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 459.0, 809.5, 338.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "Because we're using 4 different devices (1 for each video/channel), we need to keep their messages properly separated."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-62",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 406.0, 458.5, 410.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "Use positionInPixels in projectionMode 1 to be exact with your offsets. This is the main feature of syncSuite."
                }
            },
